WEBVTT

00:00:00.326 --> 00:00:06.614
This video shows how to build a question paper on a phone, from the setup to a saved draft.

00:00:08.277 --> 00:00:20.205
Tap the menu button at the top left, open Content Creation, and then choose Paper Builder. Three steps are shown at the top: Paper Setup, Paper Structure and Add Questions.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:30.850
Choose the class and the subject. The paper title fills in from them, and you can finish it, here by adding Mid-Term 2026 at the end.

00:00:38.327 --> 00:00:54.119
Tap Next to open Paper Structure. Sections are optional. Tap Next again. A Marks mismatch message appears, because no marks are set aside yet. Tap Continue, and then choose Type manually.

00:00:56.552 --> 00:01:01.664
Type the question in the box, and then tap Add Question to put it in the paper.

00:01:10.322 --> 00:01:14.546
Scroll to the bottom and tap Open Draft to save the paper.

00:01:15.926 --> 00:01:22.334
Your papers are listed under Question Papers. The new paper is saved as a draft.

00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:31.075
The paper is saved as a draft. You can open it again to keep working.
